  "title": "Family",
  "description": "Learn to talk about your family members, siblings, and loved ones in Chinese.",
  "guidebook": "### Meet the Family!\nIn Chinese, kinship titles are wonderfully specific. Unlike English, Chinese explicitly distinguishes whether a sibling is older or younger:\n- **哥哥 (gēge)**: older brother vs. **弟弟 (dìdi)**: younger brother\n- **姐姐 (jiějie)**: older sister vs. **妹妹 (mèimei)**: younger sister\n\n### Soft Second Syllables\nMost basic family words are reduplicated characters (like **妈妈 māma** and **爸爸 bàba**). In spoken Chinese, the second syllable almost always softens into a light, **neutral tone**.\n\n### Showing Possession with 的 (de)\nTo say \"my\" or \"your\", add **的 (de)** after the pronoun:\n- **我的妈妈** (*wǒ de māma*) = my mother\n- **你的哥哥** (*nǐ de gēge*) = your older brother",
